  "id": "generalized-additive-model",
  "term": "generalized additive model",
  "definition": "A generalized additive model, in this packet described as GAMLSS, is a flexible regression approach for examining how one outcome relates to one or more predictors, including non-linear relationships. It can model not only the average level of the outcome but also other aspects of its distribution, such as spread and shape.",
